From 4e2c2044981df8e7f390da46a9d5291056d7d4d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xie Hanlong <xiehanlong834@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 16:21:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: make cpu_store emit reachable and align restore event
 order

Address advisor review on #220 (3 blocking points):

- CPUOffloadingManager.prepare_store: move the cpu_store emit before
  the return so the host-residency event is actually written.
- Scheduler: emit wakeup before admission/scheduled for restored
  requests, matching the contracted wakeup -> admission -> scheduled
  chain order.
- Tests: add append-order JSONL test (test_b134_events.py) and an
  AST-based chain contract test suite (test_b134_chain_contract.py)
  covering event order, log_stats decoupling, emit reachability and
  restore_start/restore_done ordering without requiring torch/tblib.

Co-authored-by: Hermes Agent
